# libgweather -- weather lookup and the location database GNOME's Weather
# integration and gnome-shell's weather section read.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/libgweather/4.4/libgweather-4.4.4.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=7017677753cdf7d1fdc355e4bfcdb1eba8369793a8df24d241427a939cbf4283
SRC_DIR=libgweather-4.4.4

# THE PYGOBJECT EDGE IS THE INTERESTING ONE AND IT IS INVISIBLE FROM HERE.
# data/meson.build declares
#
#     locations_bin = custom_target('locations-db',
#       command: [gen_locations_variant, '@INPUT@', '@OUTPUT@' ],
#       input: files('Locations.xml'), output: '@BASENAME@.bin', install: true, ...)
#
# with no option and no guard, and build-aux/meson/gen_locations_variant.py does
# `from gi.repository import GLib`. So this package cannot be built without
# PyGObject -- a Python binding, at build time, for a weather library. That is
# why python-pygobject is packaged, and why it is declared in
# [dependencies.build] here rather than being someone else's business.
#
# BLFS ALSO LISTS GTK-3.24.50 AS REQUIRED FOR THIS PACKAGE, AND THAT IS WRONG
# for 4.4.4: the only `gtk` in its entire meson tree is the `gtk_doc` option,
# disabled below. Declaring it would have widened this tree's deliberately
# narrow GTK 3 island -- which exists for libnma alone -- for nothing. Read the
# source, not the dependency page.
#
# -Dsoup2=false is stated even though it is ALREADY THE DEFAULT HERE, and that
# is the point rather than noise: geocode-glib, packaged in the same wave from
# the same upstream for the same consumer, defaults the SAME option name to
# TRUE. Two projects one step apart, opposite defaults, and only one of them
# would have broken. Stating it in both is what makes the pair readable.
#
# -Dgtk_doc=false. Defaults TRUE, and doc/meson.build:6 then looks for gi-docgen
# -- which BLFS notes "is also provided as a meson subproject, which will be
# used if -D gtk_doc=false is not passed". Every recipe here inherits
# --wrap-mode=nodownload, so that subproject is a hard configure failure rather
# than a quiet vendored copy.
#
# -Dtests=false. Defaults TRUE; nothing here runs them.
#
# -Denable_vala=false. A combo defaulting 'auto'; vala is not packaged, so auto
# resolves off today and would switch itself on the day anyone packages it.
#
# -Dintrospection=true, stated rather than inherited: gobject-introspection is
# packaged and the typelib is what a GJS consumer resolves.
#
# NOT SET, AND DELIBERATELY: -Dzoneinfo_dir. It defaults to /usr/share/zoneinfo,
# which does not exist in this tree today -- and it does not matter, because
# libgweather/meson.build:72 only does
# `config_h.set_quoted('ZONEINFO_DIR', get_option('zoneinfo_dir'))` and NOTHING
# in 4.4.4 reads that macro. Checked by grepping the whole source tree, not just
# the meson files. Recorded because the obvious move -- pointing it somewhere
# real, or asserting the directory exists -- would be an assertion on a value
# with no consumer. (tzdata is a genuine gap in this tree; it is just not this
# package's gap.)
MESON_ARGS="-Dsoup2=false \
-Dintrospection=true \
-Denable_vala=false \
-Dgtk_doc=false \
-Dtests=false"
